# Flutter — Drawer

## 1. What is a Drawer?

A `Drawer` is a side menu that slides in from the left side of the screen.

Common uses:

* Home
* Profile
* Settings
* About
* Logout

---

## 2. Where do we add Drawer?

A Drawer is added to **Scaffold**:

```dart
Scaffold(
  appBar: AppBar(
    title: Text("Home"),
  ),

  drawer: Drawer(
    child: ...
  ),

  body: ...
)
```

### Important

You **do NOT add Drawer inside AppBar**.

The structure is:

```text
MaterialApp
    ↓
Scaffold
    ├── AppBar
    ├── Drawer
    └── Body
```

---

## 3. How does the Drawer appear in the AppBar?

When you write:

```dart
Scaffold(
  appBar: AppBar(
    title: Text("Home"),
  ),

  drawer: Drawer(
    child: ...
  ),
)
```

Flutter automatically adds the **☰ hamburger/menu button** to the AppBar.

You don't need to write:

```dart
IconButton(...)
```

for the basic Drawer.

### Example

```dart
Scaffold(
  appBar: AppBar(
    title: Text("Home"),
  ),

  drawer: Drawer(
    child: ListView(
      children: [
        DrawerHeader(
          child: Text("My App"),
        ),

        ListTile(
          leading: Icon(Icons.home),
          title: Text("Home"),
        ),

        ListTile(
          leading: Icon(Icons.settings),
          title: Text("Settings"),
        ),
      ],
    ),
  ),

  body: Center(
    child: Text("Home Screen"),
  ),
)
```

The result is roughly:

```text
┌──────────────────────────────┐
│ ☰   Home                     │
├──────────────────────────────┤
│                              │
│         Home Screen          │
│                              │
└──────────────────────────────┘
```

Tap `☰` → Drawer opens.

---

## 4. DrawerHeader

`DrawerHeader` is the top part of the Drawer.

```dart
DrawerHeader(
  child: Text("My App"),
)
```

You can put:

* App name
* Logo
* Profile image
* Username
* Email

inside it.

---

## 5. ListTile

`ListTile` is commonly used for Drawer menu items.

```dart
ListTile(
  leading: Icon(Icons.home),
  title: Text("Home"),
  onTap: () {
    Navigator.pop(context);
  },
)
```

Important properties:

```text
leading   → left icon
title     → main text
subtitle  → smaller text
trailing  → right-side widget
onTap     → what happens when clicked
```

---

## 6. Closing the Drawer

When the user taps a menu item:

```dart
Navigator.pop(context);
```

closes the Drawer.

Example:

```dart
ListTile(
  leading: Icon(Icons.settings),
  title: Text("Settings"),

  onTap: () {
    Navigator.pop(context);
  },
)
```

---

## 7. Opening Drawer manually

You can also open the Drawer using:

```dart
Scaffold.of(context).openDrawer();
```

But normally you don't need this because Flutter automatically provides the AppBar menu button.

---

## 8. Complete Example

```dart
import 'package:flutter/material.dart';

class HomeScreen extends StatelessWidget {
  const HomeScreen({super.key});

  @override
  Widget build(BuildContext context) {
    return Scaffold(
      appBar: AppBar(
        title: Text("Home"),
      ),

      drawer: Drawer(
        child: ListView(
          padding: EdgeInsets.zero,
          children: [
            DrawerHeader(
              child: Text(
                "My App",
                style: TextStyle(fontSize: 24),
              ),
            ),

            ListTile(
              leading: Icon(Icons.home),
              title: Text("Home"),
              onTap: () {
                Navigator.pop(context);
              },
            ),

            ListTile(
              leading: Icon(Icons.person),
              title: Text("Profile"),
              onTap: () {
                Navigator.pop(context);
              },
            ),

            ListTile(
              leading: Icon(Icons.settings),
              title: Text("Settings"),
              onTap: () {
                Navigator.pop(context);
              },
            ),

            ListTile(
              leading: Icon(Icons.logout),
              title: Text("Logout"),
              onTap: () {
                Navigator.pop(context);
              },
            ),
          ],
        ),
      ),

      body: Center(
        child: Text("Home Screen"),
      ),
    );
  }
}
```

## Remember

```text
Drawer → Scaffold
AppBar → automatically gets ☰
ListTile → menu item
Navigator.pop() → closes Drawer
```
